  "definition": "A ground control point (GCP) is a feature that can be identified in imagery or survey data and whose coordinates are known in the required output reference system. Its measured ground coordinates and corresponding image location constrain a geometric model. The uncertainty of both observations matters: an accurately surveyed point is poor control if the feature is ambiguous, has moved or cannot be marked consistently in the image.[^1]",
